  clock: 8  # 81ea
  nonce: 81ea  # 81ea
  message: "All Level 2 scope shipped (2026-04-23):\n- Phase 1 (PR #3313): NameMatcher utility + base_class/parent_base_class retrofit\n- Phase 2 (PR #3315): annotation/parameter_type retrofit; decorator intentionally kept on re.compile (dispatch-set triplet semantics) with regression-guard test; di_resolution.py and io_boundary.py audited as not vulnerable\n- Phase 3 (PR #3316): AST-walking matcher-boundary lint converting convention to enforcement\n- Phase 4 (PRs #3317 + #3318): polyglot call-site coverage fixture (Python) as regression instrument for WI-zigah and audit instrument for WI-mafik / Level 1b\n\nKey structural finding: the WI-pisab Level 2 invariant (terminal-fallback canonicalization at matcher boundaries) applies to *assertion-like* matchers (is-a / has-type / is-annotated-with) but NOT to *dispatch-set* matchers (decorator YAML, where bare-vs-qualified patterns are mutually exclusive). This distinction is documented in the retrofit comments, a regression test, and the AST-walking lint. Future WI-pisab-style retrofits on new matcher fields must explicitly choose a side — the lint forces the choice."  # 81ea
